            <ArticleTitle>Identification of occult active infection using PET-CT in a combined liver-kidney transplant candidate.</ArticleTitle>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1111/tid.12776</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>This case describes a patient being considered for combined liver-kidney transplantation for Caroli's disease with a failed renal transplant. A chronic septic focus could not be located with standard imaging techniques, such as ultrasonography and computed tomography. This case report highlights the observation that a retained non-functioning transplant can be the cause of fever of unknown origin and PET-CT can be useful in diagnosing these challenging cases.</AbstractText>
